    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **279 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city title-casing behavior in the owner-creation endpoint (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`).\n\n**Change** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n- In `addOwner`, after mapping the incoming fields, the city is now resolved via a new `resolveCity(...)` call before duplicate checks and customer-code generation, so the stored and returned `city` reflects the resolved value.\n- `resolveCity(String city)`: scans existing owners for one whose city matches the supplied city ignoring case; if found, reuses that owner's exact spelling. Otherwise falls back to a title-cased version. Null-safe.\n- `toTitleCase(String value)`: capitalizes the first letter of each whitespace-separated word and lower-cases the rest, preserving original spacing (e.g. `\"new york\"` / `\"NEW YORK\"` \u2192 `\"New York\"`).\n\n**Tests** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`:\n- `createOwnerTitleCasesCity`: a brand-new city (`\"west sacramento\"`) is returned as `\"West Sacramento\"`.\n- `createOwnerReusesExistingCitySpelling`: with an existing owner in `\"OldePortville\"`, creating another owner with `\"oldeportville\"` returns the existing spelling `\"OldePortville\"`.\n\nV2 has no owner-creation endpoint, so no change was needed there. Existing behavior (duplicate detection, customer code \u2014 which already upper-cases the city) is unaffected.",
